 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 36,
   "y": 20,
   "plaque": "akrotiri_dhekelia_garrison",
   "title": "Dhekelia Garrison",
   "text": "Dhekelia is the eastern Sovereign Base Area, a stretch of coast on Larnaca Bay, with a British garrison and a number of Cypriot villages inside its boundary. The garrison has existed since the 1950s, and it houses soldiers, families, schools and, like every British garrison, a very good NAAFI."
  },
  {
   "x": 32,
   "y": 40,
   "plaque": "akrotiri_dhekelia_carob",
   "title": "The Carob Tree",
   "text": "Cyprus has grown carobs for thousands of years, and the dark, sticky pods were once the island's best-known export. The tiny seeds were so regular in weight that people used them to weigh gold, and the word 'carat' comes from the Greek name for a carob seed. The tree is still all over the island, usually looking contentedly crooked."
  },
  {
   "x": 24,
   "y": 38,
   "plaque": "akrotiri_dhekelia_olive",
   "title": "The Olive Groves",
   "text": "Olive trees on Cyprus live for centuries and look it, with trunks twisted like rope. The fruit is picked by hand in autumn, and the oil is pressed within a day. A Cypriot lunch is a plate of olives, a bit of halloumi, some bread and a lot of time."
  },
  {
   "x": 54,
   "y": 40,
   "plaque": "akrotiri_dhekelia_bay",
   "title": "Larnaca Bay",
   "text": "The sea in front of Dhekelia is Larnaca Bay, warm and shallow with a bottom of fine sand. The water is clear enough to see your toes, and the beach is lined with tamarisk trees that have learned to put up with salt and wind. In the distance lies the coast of the island."
  },
  {
   "x": 4,
   "y": 20,
   "plaque": "akrotiri_dhekelia_green_line",
   "title": "The Green Line",
   "text": "Since the 1974 division of Cyprus, a United Nations buffer zone known as the Green Line has run across the island from sea to sea, patrolled by UN peacekeepers. Dhekelia lies close to the buffer zone in the east. Many Cypriots on both sides hope for a peaceful settlement, and the UN has been there for decades to help keep the peace."
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 3,
   "text": "PYLA and NICOSIA, north across the Mesaoria. The road leaves the Sovereign Base Area at the edge of the buffer zone."
  }
 ],
